{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Come on back. I'll grab your vitals real quick, the doctor's still fighting with the computer.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay. Uh, my stomach's been awful, that's why I'm here.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Blood pressure's one twenty-eight over eighty-two. Pulse seventy-six. Oxygen ninety-eight percent, and temp's ninety-eight point four.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, this update thing popped up again. Alright, what brings you in today?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, stomach pain. And I can't sleep.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): Say that one more time? I clicked the wrong window.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Stomach pain, and I'm sleeping terribly. The pain's been three weeks.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Three weeks. Whereabouts?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Middle, up under the ribs. It burns sometimes.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No fever.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): And the sleep?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): I wake up around three and then I'm just awake. I don't know, doctor, I can't say when that started. A while.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): You taking anything?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Ibuprofen. Two hundred milligrams, twice a day, for the pain.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hold on, it wiped the line. What dose, and how often?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Two hundred milligrams, twice a day. Barely does anything.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any medication allergies?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No, none.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Do you drink alcohol?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Socially.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Socially meaning?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, a bottle of wine most nights, perhaps. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Okay. No judgment from me. That amount can irritate the stomach, and it messes with sleep.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. I should take back what I said, I did throw up. Twice this week, after dinner.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Twice this week. Queasy right before that, or no?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, queasy right before.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me press on your belly. Soft, tender in the epigastrium, no guarding. Sorry, had to glance back at the screen.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): That's the spot. My parking meter's definitely expired, but whatever.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm thinking likely gastritis, or reflux, from the ibuprofen and the wine. Provisional, not definite.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Is it an ulcer? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): I can't tell that today. I'm starting omeprazole, twenty milligrams once a day, before breakfast. Swallow it whole.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hold the ibuprofen, it can make the lining worse. I'll order liver blood tests and a CBC. Get them drawn downstairs today, no fasting.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Today works.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): Come back in three weeks, we'll look at the labs and see if the omeprazole's helping. Easing up on the wine, even a little, would help too."
 ],
